 "final_text": "Submitted. Summary of the Feb 24-28 receipts reconciliation (bank operating-account statement vs. AR books, `CustomerTransactions`):\n\n- **Matched (2):** PMT-2101 Alpine Ski House wire $12,400.00 (2/24), PMT-2103 Coho Winery wire $22,000.00 (2/26) \u2014 bank and books agree exactly.\n- **Discrepancy:** PMT-2102, City Power & Light ACH (2/25) \u2014 bank shows $8,105.75 received, books recorded $8,150.75 (a $45.00 transposition-style mismatch).\n- **Bank-only:** DEP-9911, $6,750.00 (2/28), memo \"UNIDENTIFIED REMITTER \u2013 LOCKBOX\" \u2014 cash hit the bank but has no corresponding entry in books; needs to be identified and posted.\n- **Books-only:** PMT-2104, $5,325.50 (2/27), \"Check 8841 \u2013 Consolidated Messenger\" \u2014 recorded as received in books but doesn't appear on the bank statement for this window (check likely not yet cleared/deposited).\n\nNote: the bank statement also carried a large volume of `DEP-70xx`/`PMT-70xx` batch and outbound-payment lines, and books had a large volume of generic `ARPM-*` invoice payments \u2014 none of those cross-referenced by amount or reference to anything on the other side, so I treated them as unrelated background activity outside this receipts reconciliation rather than false discrepancies.",
